Inheritance

Superclass (parent)
-> Sublcass (child)

Imparts variables from Superclass to Subclass

Parent: A vehicle is representative as a parent class
Child 1: A car and a truck are types of vehicles
Child 2: Electric and Petrol are types of cars
	Child 2 is a second tier child (child of Child 1)

The Car, Truck, Electric, and Petrol classes would all inherit attributes and methods from the Vehicle class.
Ehe Electric and Petrol classes contain additional attributes and methods from the Vehicle class.

Child, also known as derived class

Keyword "Extends" in Java

Example
To indicate that the Car class is derived from the Vehicle class, we would code the following header:
	public class Car extends Vehicle{}

To indicate that the Truck class is derived from the Vehicle class, we would have the following class header for the Vehicle class:
	public class Truck extends Vehicle{}

