Polymophism
Any Java object that can pass more than one IS-A test (i.e., a parent class having two or more subclasses)
	is considered to be polymorphic.

"Poly" means many

an exmaple of polymorphism is overloading, like below. Different methods with the same name, but different parameters

	public class SimplePoly {
		public static void mymessage() {
			System.out.println("Just a simple message"); 
		}
		public static void mymessage(String msg) {
			System.out.println(msg);
		}
		public static void main(String[] args)
		{
			mymessage();
			mymessage("Simple message from Main");
		}
	}

