Interfaces
interface type
blueprint for a subclass
	Abstract and cannot be instantiated
like a template for an abstract concept
Does not have constructors
Cannot extend classes, must be implemented by them
Fields are final and cannot change

To create an interface using built-in tools
	start to create a class, select "interface"

Example:
	package interface;
	
	public interface Product {
		private String name;	//Compilation error
		//Cannot be "private"
		//Becuase fields have to be static and final, it is common to only have methods in interfaces
		
		String getName()
		void setName(String name);
		
	}


as a "standard" class, this would have been
	package interface;
	
	public class Product {
		private String name;
	}

fields in an interface are ALWAYS Static AND Final
	Implicitly Static and Final even when not declared

Classes that implement an interface would not have access to a prive field

